WEBVTT

00:01.712 --> 00:05.025
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.125 --> 00:08.411
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.445 --> 00:11.964
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.999 --> 00:14.967
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:15.002 --> 00:18.471
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.505 --> 00:21.790
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.808 --> 00:23.359
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.393 --> 00:24.727
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.761 --> 00:26.184
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.188 --> 00:37.023
All right, Drunken
Clammers, this is it,

00:37.057 --> 00:38.824
the most important
game of the season.

00:38.859 --> 00:41.260
Now, is everybody drunk?
(others react affirmatively)

00:41.294 --> 00:42.728
Completely.
Okay, good.

00:42.763 --> 00:45.531
And did nobody warm up?
(others react affirmatively)

00:45.582 --> 00:48.367
Good. 'Cause there's nothing
an unstretched middle-aged body

00:48.402 --> 00:50.186
likes more than
explosive movements.

00:50.220 --> 00:52.171
Now remember, we're here
to impress the girlfriends

00:52.205 --> 00:53.522
of guys we barely know,

00:53.557 --> 00:55.675
so when you get the ball,
throw it like a cannon.

00:55.709 --> 00:58.027
You must throw your arm out
on every play.

00:58.061 --> 01:00.029
Any other softball-related
questions?

01:00.063 --> 01:01.147
Yeah, I got a question:

01:01.181 --> 01:02.982
Can we leave
our bad-for-the-environment

01:03.016 --> 01:05.351
Styrofoam coolers behind
when we leave?

01:05.385 --> 01:06.686
Yes, you must
leave them behind,

01:06.720 --> 01:08.421
and they must be
in a crumbly mess

01:08.455 --> 01:10.356
so that the city clean-up
workers have to chase

01:10.390 --> 01:12.241
the little bits
when the wind blows.

01:12.275 --> 01:13.826
You know, Stewie, this is
actually a good park.

01:13.860 --> 01:15.711
I've found a lot
of old tennis balls here.

01:15.746 --> 01:17.179
Eh, I don't care
for this place.

01:17.214 --> 01:18.447
Last time I was here,

01:18.482 --> 01:21.083
I accidentally walked
into a Spanish picnic.

01:21.118 --> 01:24.420
Excuse me, has anyone seen
a toy car around here?

01:24.454 --> 01:26.088
<i>Ooh. Es baby.</i>

01:26.123 --> 01:27.840
I make beautiful.

01:27.874 --> 01:29.125
(clippers buzzing)

01:34.564 --> 01:36.932
Don't get any ideas
about Julio.

01:36.967 --> 01:38.934
I'm his number one.

01:38.969 --> 01:41.437
Here comes
Goldman's Pharmacy.

01:43.140 --> 01:44.373
Hey, Goldman's Pharmacy!

01:44.408 --> 01:46.892
Can you fill out a prescription
for us for diarrhea?

01:46.927 --> 01:48.477
We're about to get the runs!

01:48.512 --> 01:50.763
(others laugh)

01:50.797 --> 01:52.364
Oh, yeah?
Well, speaking of things

01:52.399 --> 01:53.866
that are brown and can run,

01:53.900 --> 01:55.801
meet our new teammate!

01:58.171 --> 02:00.156
Holy crap.
They got a ringer.

02:00.190 --> 02:02.158
What the hell?
Jerome's on your team?

02:02.192 --> 02:04.026
That's right.
We got to know each other

02:04.060 --> 02:06.362
while I was following
him around my store.

02:06.396 --> 02:08.364
What's up, fools?
I'd like to dedicate

02:08.398 --> 02:11.267
my performance today
to Miss Whitney Houston.

02:11.301 --> 02:13.302
Oh, we are (bleep).

02:17.340 --> 02:18.307
Come on, Jerome!

02:18.341 --> 02:20.076
Get a hit so I can bring

02:20.110 --> 02:21.844
a sports trophy home
for my parents!

02:21.846 --> 02:24.713
Jeffrey Lipsitz
has two soccerals!ed

02:24.748 --> 02:27.583
I can't play soccer--
I have newborn-calf ankles!

02:27.617 --> 02:29.602
You know this, damn it!

02:30.670 --> 02:32.972
I'm gonna tear the cover
off this ball.

02:33.006 --> 02:36.025
But, hang on, first I got
to adjust myself.

02:41.548 --> 02:43.699
Are you having
a nice morning, dear?

02:43.733 --> 02:47.002
Oh, yes, I love living here,
in the next town over.

02:50.891 --> 02:51.874
All right, chick batter!

02:51.908 --> 02:52.858
Everyone bring it in!

02:52.893 --> 02:53.909
Bring it on in!

02:53.944 --> 02:55.211
Get a hit, babe!

02:55.245 --> 02:57.530
(deep voice):
You know it, babe.

02:57.564 --> 03:00.382
All right, move it back!
Move it back!

03:02.586 --> 03:04.203
Peter, why do you look
so nervous?

03:04.237 --> 03:07.873
I promised a kid in the hospital
I'd hit a home run for him.

03:11.361 --> 03:12.928
Sorry, I struck
out looking.

03:12.963 --> 03:14.930
Wait, you're not
the kid I promised.

03:14.965 --> 03:16.866
No, he died last night.

03:16.900 --> 03:18.551
Oh, phew.

03:22.189 --> 03:24.106
All right, guys, one more out
and the game is ours.

03:24.141 --> 03:25.674
Come on, Horace!
Strike him out!

03:33.283 --> 03:34.066
(crowd gasps)

03:34.100 --> 03:35.684
(gasps)

03:40.640 --> 03:41.857
Horace! You okay?

03:41.891 --> 03:42.908
Oh, my God!
He's really hurt bad!

03:42.943 --> 03:44.126
You're out of the baseline,
by the way.

03:44.161 --> 03:45.244
You're out. Game's over.

03:45.278 --> 03:47.513
But, oh, my God,
Horace is really hurt.

03:48.598 --> 03:50.032
He's dead.

03:50.066 --> 03:51.734
(all gasp, murmur)

03:51.768 --> 03:54.203
Let him rest in peace.

03:56.306 --> 03:58.390
(sighs) Let's put
some leaves on him

03:58.425 --> 04:00.259
and go get some ice cream.

04:06.733 --> 04:08.701
I can't believe Horace is dead.

04:08.735 --> 04:12.271
I can't believe we left Brian
in the car with the windows up.

04:13.306 --> 04:15.274
I'm gonna pee!

04:15.308 --> 04:17.943
Listen, I just
feel awful about this.

04:17.978 --> 04:20.479
Horace was a good bartender
and a good guy.

04:20.513 --> 04:22.498
I wish there was something
I could do.

04:22.532 --> 04:24.466
Well, we know you
didn't mean it, Jerome.

04:24.501 --> 04:26.068
It's just a
terrible situation.

04:26.102 --> 04:28.020
Like when you're the
only one at the table

04:28.054 --> 04:29.955
where the waiter doesn't
say, "Good order."

04:29.990 --> 04:32.291
I'll have the halibut.
Ah, great choice.

04:32.325 --> 04:34.460
One of the chef's specialties;
you'll love it.

04:34.494 --> 04:36.962
It was caught fresh less
than ten miles from here.

04:36.997 --> 04:38.631
I'll have the New York
strip steak.

04:38.665 --> 04:40.699
Mmm! My absolute
favorite dish here.

04:40.734 --> 04:43.369
It is a spectacular cut,
superbly seasoned

04:43.403 --> 04:46.205
and the marbling is some
of the best I've ever seen.

04:46.239 --> 04:47.473
And I'll have
the chicken.

04:47.507 --> 04:49.008
Mm-hmm.

04:50.710 --> 04:52.177
Good afternoon.

04:52.212 --> 04:53.846
I'd just like to say that...

04:53.880 --> 04:56.682
before today, I didn't know
the Munsters were driving around

04:56.716 --> 04:58.183
in a funeral car.

04:58.218 --> 05:00.586
I'm beginning to think
everything on that show

05:00.620 --> 05:02.621
was a big joke.

05:04.224 --> 05:06.191
(inhales deeply)

05:06.226 --> 05:09.361
(voice quavering):
I'd, um... I'd just like...

05:09.396 --> 05:11.730
(gasps)

05:11.765 --> 05:13.766
Whe... When you lose...

05:13.800 --> 05:15.701
(stifled sobs)

05:15.735 --> 05:17.703
(sniffles, exhales)

05:17.737 --> 05:20.839
(high-pitched): Um, there's
so... There's so mu...

05:20.874 --> 05:23.575
(exhales)
There's so much...

05:23.610 --> 05:26.996
(grunts)

05:27.030 --> 05:29.999
I... I...

05:30.033 --> 05:31.667
(sobbing)

05:31.685 --> 05:33.335
Thank you, Quagmire.

05:33.370 --> 05:36.972
<i>Perhaps there are some men who
would like to say a few words.</i>

05:37.007 --> 05:39.975
Horace owned the Clam
for over 30 years.

05:40.010 --> 05:42.945
During that time,
he touched all of our lives.

05:42.979 --> 05:45.614
He was a great bartender
and a great friend.

05:45.649 --> 05:48.133
And so let us take
a look back on his life

05:48.168 --> 05:51.019
through this video
commemorating all the DUI's

05:51.037 --> 05:53.405
that he was responsible for.

05:56.176 --> 06:03.215
♪ I will remember you

06:03.249 --> 06:09.505
♪ Will you remember me?

06:09.539 --> 06:13.225
♪ Don't let your life

06:13.259 --> 06:15.594
♪ Pass you by

06:15.645 --> 06:17.730
E.T.:
Ouch.

06:17.764 --> 06:19.898
Is there a bathroom in here?

06:19.933 --> 06:23.485
I've been yo-yoing a turd
for the last 20 minutes.

06:29.259 --> 06:30.159
(gasps)
Oh, sorry.

06:30.193 --> 06:31.560
I was looking
for the bathroom.

06:31.594 --> 06:33.395
I shouldn't have left
the door open.

06:33.430 --> 06:35.130
Sorry if you're grossed out
by this.

06:35.165 --> 06:36.565
No. No, no, I'm just...

06:36.599 --> 06:40.369
not used to seeing corpses
that big and not in a toilet.

06:40.403 --> 06:42.538
Oh, here, let me
help you with that.

06:42.572 --> 06:44.540
(grunts)

06:44.574 --> 06:45.924
There you go.

06:45.959 --> 06:47.843
Now you're all set
for your big day.

06:47.877 --> 06:50.996
Thanks. You know, I could use
some part-time help here

06:51.031 --> 06:52.831
preparing the bodies,
if you're interested.

06:52.866 --> 06:54.833
Really? Yeah,
that'd-that'd be great.

06:54.868 --> 06:56.068
I could use the money,

06:56.102 --> 06:58.420
and I'm getting kind of
tired of my old job.

06:58.455 --> 07:01.056
ANNOUNCER: Only a half a point divides
our top two competitors

07:01.091 --> 07:03.959
as we enter the last event,
the Meg Roll.

07:07.430 --> 07:08.981
You think it's cool
to go drinking

07:09.032 --> 07:10.199
right after Horace's funeral?

07:10.233 --> 07:12.368
Of course. It's what
he would've wanted.

07:12.402 --> 07:13.952
Listen, we all
got to move on.

07:13.987 --> 07:17.956
Like the Secret Service did
on November 23, 1963.

07:17.991 --> 07:19.808
All right, guys,
I know that yesterday

07:19.843 --> 07:21.143
was a rough one for us.

07:21.177 --> 07:22.444
But it's with great pride

07:22.479 --> 07:25.047
that I'm gonna turn this zero
into a one.

07:25.081 --> 07:26.248
All right!

07:26.282 --> 07:28.333
Nichols, you should
go home and change.

07:30.637 --> 07:32.037
What the hell?
Hey, pal, what're you doing?

07:32.072 --> 07:33.038
This is our bar.

07:33.073 --> 07:34.139
Not anymore.

07:34.174 --> 07:35.974
Horace owed more
than this place is worth,

07:36.009 --> 07:37.509
so it's the bank's now.

07:37.544 --> 07:40.512
I'm sorry but The Drunken Clam
is permanently closed.

07:40.547 --> 07:41.814
Closed?!

07:41.848 --> 07:43.816
<i>PETER: That was the start
of the dark times.</i>

07:43.850 --> 07:47.603
<i>The banks took our bars, our
businesses and then our homes.</i>

07:47.637 --> 07:49.104
<i>A change had to be made.</i>

07:49.138 --> 07:51.607
<i>A change only one man
could make.</i>

07:51.641 --> 07:53.625
<i>I am the Wind Maker...</i>

07:54.627 --> 07:56.495
<i>...and I shoot monkeys now.</i>

08:02.959 --> 08:06.295
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return
to Joanie Loves Chris Brown.</i>

08:06.329 --> 08:07.296
(indistinct chatter)

08:07.330 --> 08:08.964
Joanie! Chris!

08:08.999 --> 08:11.517
Welcome to the party.
Can I offer you some punch?

08:11.551 --> 08:13.852
No, thanks. I had
some in the car.

08:13.887 --> 08:15.888
<i>ANNOUNCER: Joanie Loves
Chris Brown was taped in front</i>

08:15.922 --> 08:18.123
<i>of a very uncomfortable
studio audience.</i>

08:18.158 --> 08:20.626
Man, it really sucks
they closed down the Clam.

08:20.660 --> 08:22.194
Yeah, but I... I mean,
this is good, right?

08:22.228 --> 08:24.613
I mean, as long as we got a
place to drink and a restroom

08:24.648 --> 08:26.949
for businessmen to have
homosexual encounters.

08:26.983 --> 08:28.334
Hey, thanks for the sex.

08:28.368 --> 08:31.370
Thank you for notarizing
those documents.

08:31.421 --> 08:33.389
Peter, what's
going on down here?

08:33.423 --> 08:35.491
Why are there beer bottles
all over the floor?

08:35.525 --> 08:37.559
Well, we needed a new spot
to drink, Lois.

08:37.594 --> 08:38.978
Forget it, Peter.

08:39.012 --> 08:40.546
You're not turning our
living room into a bar.

08:40.580 --> 08:42.898
Oh, come on, Lois, we got
to have a place to drink.

08:42.932 --> 08:44.049
Drinking is the only thing

08:44.084 --> 08:45.184
holding this friendship
together.

08:45.218 --> 08:48.053
Everything we try to do sober
just ends badly.

08:48.088 --> 08:51.056
I just don't think a good way
to start a screenplay is,

08:51.091 --> 08:53.726
"400 years ago
in Bethesda, Maryland."

08:53.760 --> 08:55.961
Yeah, and don't you think it's
confusing that every character

08:55.996 --> 08:58.480
in the movie is named Movie Guy?
Come on, you guys.

08:58.515 --> 09:00.799
The Oscars are next week,
so let's get this done.

09:05.705 --> 09:08.273
Meg, I'm needed upstairs,
so I'll let you finish up.

09:08.308 --> 09:10.009
Just put some blush
here and here.

09:10.043 --> 09:13.362
It makes the eyes look
a little less dead and hollow.

09:13.380 --> 09:15.180
Wow, that really works.

09:15.215 --> 09:17.583
Hmm. Maybe I'll try
that on myself.

09:17.617 --> 09:21.954
Oh, uh... you have what we call
a "closed casket face."

09:23.239 --> 09:25.140
Hey, Meg,
who's your date?

09:25.175 --> 09:27.609
He looks like a real stiff.
(laughs)

09:27.644 --> 09:29.678
Chris, what the hell
are you doing here?

09:29.713 --> 09:31.680
I told you not to
bother me at work.

09:31.715 --> 09:34.316
I got locked out of the house,
and I need your key.

09:34.351 --> 09:38.320
No way! You get to work
with all these dead people?

09:38.355 --> 09:40.689
Hey, look,
this guy's picking his nose.

09:40.724 --> 09:41.924
(laughs)

09:41.958 --> 09:43.275
Look, now he's eating it!

09:43.326 --> 09:44.643
Chris! Knock it off!

09:44.677 --> 09:46.412
You're gonna get me
in trouble!

09:46.446 --> 09:47.730
Meg, they're dead.

09:47.764 --> 09:49.565
Would you stop being so uptight?

09:49.599 --> 09:51.300
You're like one
of those Asian-Americans

09:51.334 --> 09:52.968
who fought in Vietnam.

09:53.002 --> 09:54.303
(shouts)

09:54.337 --> 09:56.305
Oh, it's just me.

09:59.976 --> 10:02.094
Peter, I thought you were taking
us to a new drinking spot.

10:02.128 --> 10:03.796
What are we doing at the Clam?
Look, guys,

10:03.830 --> 10:06.248
we tried other bars,
we tried drinking at home,

10:06.282 --> 10:07.816
we even tried the big
end-of-the-year

10:07.851 --> 10:10.219
high school party
that will change everything.

10:10.253 --> 10:11.887
If we don't lose our
virginity tonight,

10:11.921 --> 10:13.555
we're never gonna
make it in college!

10:13.590 --> 10:14.990
Hey, where's Peter?

10:15.024 --> 10:18.243
Only talking to Amanda Small,
the hottest girl in school.

10:18.278 --> 10:20.412
But aren't you going out
with Joanne Fuller?

10:20.447 --> 10:23.348
JoJo? No, she's my neighbor.
I've known her forever.

10:23.383 --> 10:24.917
She works at her dad's garage.

10:24.951 --> 10:26.418
She's practically a guy.

10:26.453 --> 10:28.654
(gasps)
JoJo?!

10:28.688 --> 10:31.490
♪ Looking from
a window above... ♪

10:31.541 --> 10:33.008
Hi, Peter.

10:33.042 --> 10:35.944
But I thought you was workin'
on your garbage sculpture.

10:35.979 --> 10:38.680
There was someone
I had to see first.

10:38.715 --> 10:41.016
Sorry, Amanda.
By the law of '80s movies,

10:41.050 --> 10:42.785
a newly transformed tomboy

10:42.819 --> 10:45.454
supersedes your
long-standing hotness.

10:46.439 --> 10:50.409
♪ And all I ever knew

10:50.443 --> 10:52.144
♪ Only you...

10:52.178 --> 10:54.179
♪

10:56.282 --> 10:58.584
Let's face it-- there's only
one drinking spot for us,

10:58.618 --> 11:00.452
and it's the Clam.
But, Peter, it's closed.

11:00.487 --> 11:01.653
We can't go in there.

11:01.688 --> 11:03.368
Quagmire, when a girl
says she doesn't want

11:03.389 --> 11:05.908
to have sex with you,
do you take that as an answer?

11:07.143 --> 11:09.828
My lawyer has advised me
not to answer that question.

11:09.863 --> 11:12.197
Look, I bet you could squeeze
through that window.

11:12.966 --> 11:14.099
(garbage can clatters)

11:14.134 --> 11:15.234
(window creaks)

11:15.268 --> 11:16.368
It's not even locked.

11:16.402 --> 11:18.203
And all the booze
is still in there.

11:18.238 --> 11:19.905
Come on, guys,
this is trespassing

11:19.939 --> 11:21.173
and it's against the law.

11:21.207 --> 11:23.108
Maybe we should
just let the Clam go

11:23.143 --> 11:24.543
and, I don't know,
spend more time

11:24.577 --> 11:25.544
with our families.

11:25.578 --> 11:26.545
Yeah, I tried that.

11:26.579 --> 11:28.147
I just spend most of the time

11:28.181 --> 11:30.149
testing Chris to see
if he's autistic.

11:32.085 --> 11:33.051
(screams):
No!

11:33.102 --> 11:34.386
(groaning, whimpering)

11:34.437 --> 11:36.672
Not overly affectionate.

11:36.706 --> 11:39.074
Guys, this is where we belong.

11:39.108 --> 11:40.843
Yeah, no question
about that.

11:40.877 --> 11:42.010
Yeah, we got roots here.

11:42.045 --> 11:44.012
We've been coming
to this place for 15 years.

11:44.047 --> 11:45.597
Our roots go back
further than that.

11:45.632 --> 11:47.099
My grandfather
used to bring me here

11:47.133 --> 11:48.267
when I was a kid.

11:48.301 --> 11:50.135
And his grandfather
brought him here.

11:54.924 --> 11:56.558
Good day, gentlemen!

11:56.593 --> 11:57.876
Welcome to the Drunken Clam!

11:57.911 --> 11:59.912
Can I get you boys
a mug of stout?

11:59.946 --> 12:01.146
Why, certainly.

12:01.181 --> 12:02.748
This is a bully establishment
you've got here.

12:02.782 --> 12:03.942
The doors are a little short,

12:03.967 --> 12:04.933
but that's okay,

12:04.968 --> 12:07.035
because we're smaller back now.

12:08.755 --> 12:09.755
To the Clam!

12:09.806 --> 12:11.039
ALL:
Hear, hear!

12:11.074 --> 12:13.876
And to brain-damaging
venereal disease.

12:13.910 --> 12:15.961
I wake up with blood
on my penis pillow.

12:15.995 --> 12:16.962
I'm gonna go insane

12:16.996 --> 12:19.231
in a wheelchair,
staring at the sea.

12:22.235 --> 12:24.336
(slurring):
This is everything about..

12:24.370 --> 12:25.771
if it's the Clam, I love it.

12:25.805 --> 12:26.939
(sighs)

12:26.973 --> 12:28.540
(slurring): I was just
gonna... that's exactly.

12:28.575 --> 12:30.342
Hey, uh, remember...
remember-remember when...

12:30.376 --> 12:34.313
remember when... remember
when Quicktime here

12:34.347 --> 12:36.431
passed out in this...
in this booth...

12:36.466 --> 12:38.500
this booth,
and we did stuff to him

12:38.535 --> 12:41.453
that you do to ladies
and we-we promised

12:41.487 --> 12:42.721
we'd never tell you.

12:42.755 --> 12:43.889
Wha...?

12:43.923 --> 12:45.290
To the Clam!

12:45.325 --> 12:49.745
Joe, you-- wha...
your hair looks stupid.

12:49.779 --> 12:51.346
All... all the greatest...

12:51.381 --> 12:53.115
all the greatest
moments of my life,

12:53.149 --> 12:55.951
I spent right here
in-in this booth.

12:55.985 --> 12:57.553
Maggie's first word.

12:57.587 --> 12:59.655
Bart jumping that canyon.

12:59.689 --> 13:00.789
Mr. Plow.

13:00.823 --> 13:03.025
All the greatest
moments of my life.

13:03.059 --> 13:04.977
Why is... why is Label Guy

13:05.011 --> 13:06.778
trying to punch me?

13:06.813 --> 13:09.915
(grumbles)
Punch you first, Label Guy.

13:09.949 --> 13:11.099
I got to go pee.

13:11.134 --> 13:12.935
(mumbles):
I don't want to get up.

13:12.969 --> 13:14.469
Joe, where's the... that thing?

13:14.504 --> 13:16.405
Where's the thing?
Where's the catheter thing?

13:16.439 --> 13:17.873
No, it's mine,
it's private.

13:17.907 --> 13:20.242
Hey, what happens
if I blow in this end?

13:20.276 --> 13:21.610
Don't, I'll 'splode.

13:21.644 --> 13:23.512
I'm gonna.

13:25.315 --> 13:28.083
You do it better
than Bonnie.

13:28.117 --> 13:31.470
It takes a man
to know what a man likes.

13:35.842 --> 13:37.809
Meg, the Dougan family
called and they now want

13:37.844 --> 13:40.112
Mr. Dougan in a gray suit
for the wake tomorrow.

13:40.146 --> 13:41.546
<i>'Cause it so matters.</i>

13:41.581 --> 13:43.015
Could you change
his suit, please?

13:43.049 --> 13:45.984
Sure.
I'll be back in a bit.

13:47.270 --> 13:48.236
(casket lid creaks)

13:48.271 --> 13:51.540
Oh... my... God!

13:51.574 --> 13:53.508
All right, Chris,
where is it?

13:53.543 --> 13:55.177
And don't try to act like

13:55.211 --> 13:56.778
you don't know what
I'm talking about.

13:56.813 --> 13:58.447
Fine, you caught me.

13:58.481 --> 14:00.248
So I borrowed your bra.

14:00.266 --> 14:02.801
My boobs hurt when I
go down the stairs!

14:02.835 --> 14:04.202
No, not that, you idiot.

14:04.237 --> 14:05.737
Where is the dead body?

14:05.772 --> 14:07.272
I know you took it.

14:07.307 --> 14:09.141
And don't lie, or I'll
tell Jennifer Connelly

14:09.175 --> 14:10.815
that you're the one
who's been mailing her

14:10.843 --> 14:11.910
those dog heads.

14:11.944 --> 14:15.213
Uh, yes, I'd like
to mail this to a whore.

14:15.248 --> 14:16.848
Okay, fine, Meg!

14:16.883 --> 14:19.151
I used the body to get me
into R-rated movies.

14:19.185 --> 14:20.552
After that,
I took him swimming

14:20.586 --> 14:21.853
and he fell apart.

14:21.888 --> 14:24.122
Chris, Mr. Dougan's
wake is tomorrow,

14:24.157 --> 14:26.858
and there's going to be
a body in that casket.

14:26.893 --> 14:29.261
If it's not his,
it's going to be yours.

14:29.295 --> 14:31.113
Hey, guys,
what's goin' on?

14:31.147 --> 14:32.714
And no one says anything,

14:32.749 --> 14:35.200
which means they hate it.

14:39.489 --> 14:42.090
Oh, God.

14:42.125 --> 14:44.092
I am so hung over.

14:44.127 --> 14:45.260
(groans):
Me, too.

14:45.294 --> 14:46.828
But luckily,
when I'm hung over,

14:46.863 --> 14:48.764
I can just molt
into another Peter.

14:48.798 --> 14:51.833
(grunting)

14:51.868 --> 14:53.368
Wow, that's amazing.

14:53.403 --> 14:54.870
Yeah, but for the next
ten minutes,

14:54.904 --> 14:56.538
I'll be very vulnerable
to predators.

14:56.572 --> 14:57.539
(growling)

14:57.573 --> 14:58.540
(gasps)
Mountain lion.

14:58.574 --> 14:59.741
Make yourself look big!

14:59.776 --> 15:01.476
(growls)

15:03.346 --> 15:04.446
(engines rumbling)

15:04.480 --> 15:05.480
What the hell?

15:07.116 --> 15:08.984
There's a bunch
of bulldozers out there.

15:09.018 --> 15:11.002
(engines rumbling)

15:14.741 --> 15:16.625
Hold it, hold it!
What-what's going on?

15:16.659 --> 15:18.009
We're here to
demolish this building

15:18.044 --> 15:19.644
by order of the bank.

15:19.679 --> 15:21.012
Like hell you are!

15:21.047 --> 15:23.648
Wh-What are you
talking about, Peter?

15:23.683 --> 15:25.517
We ain't goin' nowhere.

15:25.551 --> 15:27.502
This bar belongs to us.

15:27.537 --> 15:29.304
(ice cream truck chiming)

15:29.338 --> 15:31.406
(gasps)
Ice cream truck!

15:33.176 --> 15:34.609
You didn't get any ice cream?

15:34.644 --> 15:36.311
The ice cream man
was handsome.

15:36.345 --> 15:37.612
I got nervous.

15:46.718 --> 15:47.868
We interrupt this program

15:47.903 --> 15:50.004
for a Channel Five
breaking news report.

15:50.038 --> 15:52.640
Three local men
have barricaded themselves

15:52.674 --> 15:54.442
inside a Quahog bar,
and are currently

15:54.476 --> 15:56.110
in a standoff with authorities.

15:56.144 --> 15:57.845
We now go live to Joyce Kinney,

15:57.879 --> 16:00.214
who attended her sister's
wedding last night.

16:00.248 --> 16:01.215
Thanks, Tom.

16:01.249 --> 16:02.383
One of the suspects has been

16:02.417 --> 16:04.118
identified as Peter Griffin.

16:04.152 --> 16:05.453
But the real story is,

16:05.487 --> 16:06.637
I'd be married, too,

16:06.655 --> 16:08.606
if I were willing
to date a Persian.

16:08.640 --> 16:09.874
Guys, they found him.

16:09.908 --> 16:11.292
Don't bother
with the posters.

16:11.326 --> 16:12.827
My God,
what is Peter thinking?!

16:12.861 --> 16:15.196
Yes, he's crazy as
a serial killer.

16:15.230 --> 16:17.598
All right, what do you
want for your last meal?

16:17.632 --> 16:19.734
Uh, I think I'll
just have a salad.

16:19.768 --> 16:20.801
Dressing on the side.

16:20.836 --> 16:23.137
<i>I had a huge last lunch.</i>

16:26.308 --> 16:27.892
All right, listen up in there!

16:27.926 --> 16:30.494
Let's not make this
any harder than it has to be.

16:30.512 --> 16:32.546
We have a lot of dumb cops here.

16:32.581 --> 16:33.698
Guys, this is crazy.

16:33.732 --> 16:34.632
Plus, I'm a cop.

16:34.666 --> 16:36.067
I can't be a part of this.

16:36.101 --> 16:37.885
Come on, Joe, this is our bar.

16:37.919 --> 16:40.121
It's where the three of us
made that suicide pact

16:40.155 --> 16:42.790
that Quagmire and I are gonna
back out of at the last minute.

16:42.824 --> 16:44.959
I'm sorry, guys,
but it's my job.

16:44.993 --> 16:47.395
I got a family to support.

16:47.446 --> 16:48.446
That jerk!

16:48.480 --> 16:49.613
How could he desert us?

16:49.648 --> 16:51.415
Relax, Quagmire,
he's just doing his job.

16:51.450 --> 16:52.683
You'll forgive him.

16:52.718 --> 16:54.952
Just like Kathleen Turner
forgave her mirror.

16:54.986 --> 16:55.986
Sorry.

16:56.021 --> 16:58.155
Turns out you were
right about me.

17:00.559 --> 17:01.792
LOIS:
Officer, wait!

17:01.827 --> 17:04.528
I'm his wife;
give me that bullhorn.

17:04.563 --> 17:06.464
Peter, you get out here
right now,

17:06.498 --> 17:08.065
or else I'm throwing away

17:08.100 --> 17:11.168
all of your
Mr. Potato Heads, I swear.

17:11.203 --> 17:13.871
It's okay, she only knows
where the decoys are.

17:13.905 --> 17:15.823
Swanson, there you are.

17:15.857 --> 17:17.675
Listen, you hang out
at this dump.

17:17.709 --> 17:19.960
I want you to go in there
and end this thing.

17:19.995 --> 17:21.262
I'll do my best, sir.

17:26.217 --> 17:27.601
<i>PETER:
This is our bar.</i>

17:27.652 --> 17:30.070
<i>It's the cornerstone
of our friendship.</i>

17:30.105 --> 17:31.655
<i>TIM GUNN:
Joe, this is Tim Gunn.</i>

17:31.690 --> 17:33.157
<i>I agree with your friend.</i>

17:33.191 --> 17:36.143
I got to get that guy
out of my head.

17:36.178 --> 17:38.112
Look, they're sending Joe in.

17:38.146 --> 17:40.498
All right, listen up, fellas.

17:40.532 --> 17:42.767
Joe, wait, put your gun down.

17:42.801 --> 17:44.869
There's no point
in fighting anymore.

17:44.903 --> 17:46.837
We'll leave quietly.

17:46.872 --> 17:48.339
Like hell you will.

17:48.373 --> 17:49.607
This is our Clam,

17:49.641 --> 17:52.543
<i>and we are not
gonna let them take it.</i>

17:52.577 --> 17:55.045
Yay! All right!
All right! Yeah!

17:56.047 --> 17:58.065
We love Joe!

17:58.099 --> 18:00.785
Swanson, what the hell's
going on in here?

18:00.819 --> 18:02.069
I'm sorry, Chief.

18:02.103 --> 18:04.572
I just can't let them
bulldoze this building.

18:04.606 --> 18:06.207
Hey, Joe, is this
the same chief

18:06.241 --> 18:07.842
whose wife is a real hog?

18:07.876 --> 18:09.343
Swanson, don't be a fool.

18:09.377 --> 18:11.712
You really want to throw away
your career on this?

18:11.746 --> 18:13.481
Guys, your bar is gone.

18:13.515 --> 18:14.982
And since
it's bank property,

18:15.016 --> 18:18.269
I have no choice but to place
you all under arrest.

18:18.303 --> 18:20.738
JEROME: It ain't
bank property no more.

18:23.475 --> 18:25.509
Jerome?!
What are you doing here?

18:25.544 --> 18:27.211
Listen, it's kind of
all my fault

18:27.245 --> 18:28.679
this happened
in the first place.

18:28.713 --> 18:31.182
I'm responsible
for Horace's death.

18:31.216 --> 18:33.384
Plus, as a former athlete,
it's my responsibility

18:33.418 --> 18:36.821
to invest my earnings
in a restaurant, bar,

18:36.855 --> 18:37.988
or car dealership.

18:38.023 --> 18:39.323
What sport did you play?

18:39.357 --> 18:40.324
Lacrosse.

18:40.358 --> 18:42.359
Which is also
my brother's name.

18:42.394 --> 18:44.495
Look, I felt bad
about what I did to Horace.

18:44.529 --> 18:46.263
So, when I heard on the news

18:46.298 --> 18:47.731
that they were tearing down
his bar,

18:47.766 --> 18:51.035
I saw buying it as a way
to carry on Horace's legacy.

18:51.069 --> 18:53.470
So I own the Clam now.

18:53.505 --> 18:55.573
Chief, you can call
off your cops.

18:55.607 --> 18:58.475
And you can send those
bulldozers home.

18:58.510 --> 19:00.144
Yay, the Clam is saved!

19:00.178 --> 19:02.012
(cheering)
Yeah! All right.

19:02.047 --> 19:03.280
We pulled it off, guys.

19:03.315 --> 19:04.598
Oh, thank God.

19:04.633 --> 19:06.500
And all because
I believed in myself

19:06.535 --> 19:08.536
like Pop-Pop always said.

19:08.587 --> 19:10.621
Please give me rat poison,

19:10.655 --> 19:12.623
I want only to die.

19:12.657 --> 19:15.643
No, we did it, Pop-Pop.

19:18.847 --> 19:20.598
Meg, the family is here

19:20.632 --> 19:21.782
for Mr. Dougan's wake,

19:21.816 --> 19:24.168
so could you please
bring in the body?

19:24.202 --> 19:26.337
Meg, I'm not doing this.

19:26.371 --> 19:27.504
You have to, Chris.

19:27.539 --> 19:29.590
Siblings have to look
out for each other.

19:29.624 --> 19:30.958
Like the Mannings.

19:30.992 --> 19:33.427
Eli, you threw
for three touchdowns today,

19:33.461 --> 19:36.163
which isn't bad,
except Peyton had four.

19:36.197 --> 19:38.799
Well, Cooper got pre-approved
for a Visa card today.

19:38.833 --> 19:41.468
Come on, guys,
we all had a good day.

19:46.174 --> 19:47.474
Stop it.

19:47.509 --> 19:48.776
I have an itch.

19:48.810 --> 19:50.244
I don't care.

19:50.278 --> 19:52.079
Dead people don't
scratch their balls.

19:52.113 --> 19:53.330
Well, I can't help it.

19:53.365 --> 19:54.865
It's these damn wool pants.

19:54.900 --> 19:56.216
I'm going bananas.

19:56.251 --> 19:58.419
If I can't scratch them,
you have to.

19:58.453 --> 20:00.087
Shh!

20:02.557 --> 20:05.292
Just, uh, straightening out
his pants a little.

20:05.327 --> 20:07.561
CHRIS: Oh, yeah...
yeah, that's good.

20:07.596 --> 20:09.563
Scratch it. Scratch it.

20:09.598 --> 20:11.532
Oh, thank you.

20:11.566 --> 20:14.268
Hello, I'm Helen Dougan.

20:14.302 --> 20:16.387
My husband had filled out
an organ donor card

20:16.421 --> 20:17.588
before he passed away,

20:17.622 --> 20:21.325
and a woman just lost
her face in a freak accident.

20:24.829 --> 20:28.832
Meg, though you cannot tell,
I am frowning.

20:32.203 --> 20:33.871
Wow, Jerome, the
place looks great.

20:33.905 --> 20:35.906
Yeah, look at you,
owning a bar.

20:35.941 --> 20:37.541
You guys are doing
pretty good.

20:37.575 --> 20:39.476
First you get to run
Somalia, now this.

20:39.511 --> 20:40.611
Well, it sure is good

20:40.645 --> 20:42.179
to be back in the old Clam.

20:42.213 --> 20:44.515
Hey, there's some guys
sitting in our booth.

20:46.117 --> 20:48.118
Maybe we should tell them
it's our booth.

20:48.153 --> 20:50.522
Uh-huh. Or we could
just sit on the floor,

20:50.547 --> 20:51.837
next to these garbage cans.

20:51.838 --> 21:52.838
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru